# entire review redesign — Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use `superpowers:subagent-driven-development` (if subagents available) or `superpowers:executing-plans` to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Restructure `entire review` around subcommands + role-based agent assignment + live tokens + inline prompts. Replace the multi-click first-run setup, derive the fix agent from roles (drop the "Choose fix agent" prompt), surface live token counts during runs, and add an inline `[Y]es · [s]elect fixes · [n]o · [A]lways` prompt at the end of every review.

**Architecture:**
- New `entire review setup` cobra subcommand owns first-run + edit-config. Two-step picker: pick a role for each installed agent (Reviewer / Fixer / Both / Skip), then pick skills only for Reviewer/Both.
- `entire review` becomes a runner with no inline picker. Adds `--reviewers <list>` and `--fixer <name>` flags as first-class one-off overrides — calling agents translate user intent ("you and Claude review, you fix") into a concrete invocation. Flags also work on `entire review fix`. Resolution decision tree:
   1. `--reviewers` / `--fixer` flags passed → use those (one-off, not persisted).
   2. Saved config exists → use it.
   3. Interactive, no config, no flags → print `Run: entire review setup` and exit non-zero.
   4. Non-interactive, no config, no flags, invoking agent detected (`CLAUDE_CODE`, `CODEX`, `GEMINI_CLI`, etc. env sentinels) → use that agent as both Reviewer and Fixer (Role `Both`). Emit one-line note: *Note: claude as reviewer + fixer (no config). Customize with `entire review setup`, or tell your agent who should review/fix.*
   5. Non-interactive, no config, no flags, no invoking agent (CI/pipe) → hard error.
- Recursion guard: if `ENTIRE_REVIEW_SESSION` is already set in env, `entire review` refuses to start a nested review. Prevents fan-out loops when a reviewer agent's prompt tries to re-invoke review.
- Always included context (regardless of mode): branch diff vs scope base ref, session metadata, and checkpoint context for the current commit. The `--prompt "..."` flag and the inline ask both add *additional* context on top of that baseline.
- Inline per-run-prompt ask is skipped when non-interactive; `--prompt "..."` bypasses regardless. The inline post-run fix prompt is also skipped when non-interactive — prints a `Run:` pointer block instead (or, if `--fixer` was omitted: *"Findings ready. To apply: re-run with `--fixer <agent>`, or browse: `entire review findings`."*).
- Settings schema gains a `role` field per agent in `ReviewConfig`, a `FixAfterReview` mode on `EntireSettings`, and an idempotent in-memory migration on load that derives roles from the legacy `ReviewFixAgent` field. Migration is persisted as a side effect the next time `entire review setup` (or any code path that writes settings) runs — no auto-write on Load.
- Claude/Codex reviewers emit `Tokens` events on every stream envelope that carries `usage`, not just at end-of-run.

**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, github.com/spf13/cobra, charm.land/huh/v2, github.com/go-git/go-git/v6, github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/{review, settings, agent}.

**Design reference:** `~/Desktop/entire-review-design.html` (saved 2026-05-20) — 8-scene click-through mockup of the chosen flow. Hand this to the implementing subagent for visual context.

---

## File Structure

**Modify:**
- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go` — add `Role` type + constants, add `Role` field to `ReviewConfig`, add `FixAfterReview` field to `EntireSettings` and `ClonePreferences`, extend `mergeRawSettings`, run in-memory role migration in `Load`. Add a public `Save(ctx, *EntireSettings) error` helper.
- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go` — extend roundtrip tests for the new fields.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd.go` — drop the first-run auto-picker branch in `runReview`; add `--prompt`, `--reviewers`, `--fixer` flags; wire `setup` subcommand; drop multi-agent picker dispatch (roles handle that); add `detectInvokingAgent` + recursion guard; delegate to `post_review.go` for inline post-run UX.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/picker.go` — delete `RunReviewConfigPicker`, `ConfirmFirstRunSetup`, `pickReviewFixAgentPreference`, `promptForReviewFixAgent`, `reviewFixAgentChoices`, `reviewFixAgentChoicesFromSources`, `reviewFixAgentChoice`, `defaultReviewFixAgentPick`, `savedReviewFixAgentPick`. Keep `MergePickerResults`, `SaveReviewConfig`, `SaveReviewFixAgent`, `BuildReviewPickerFields` (still used by setup until Task 2.3 supersedes it), `ComputeEligibleConfigured`, `computeLaunchableEligible`, `PromptForAgent`, `SelectReviewAgent`, `VerifyConfiguredSkillsInstalled`, `SplitSavedPicks`.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/fix.go` — derive fix agent from roles; drop the spawn-time fix-agent picker; accept `--prompt "..."` on `entire review fix`; consolidate the "Run later" footer into a single `Run:` block with three pointers.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/multipicker.go` — **delete** (the multi-agent picker is obsolete; roles answer "which agents review" up front).
- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer.go` — emit `Tokens{}` on every envelope carrying `usage` (not only on `result`). Also delete the stale "summing would double-count" comment around line 55-58 — Claude's per-assistant `usage` IS cumulative for the active turn, which the new emission proves.
- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer.go` — emit `Tokens{}` on each `item.completed` envelope whose top-level `Usage` is populated. No struct change required.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review_bridge.go` — drop the bridge for the legacy multi-agent picker; setup is registered inline in `cmd.go` (no `Deps.SetupCmd` field).
- `CLAUDE.md` — update the `entire review` section to describe the new surface, role model, and inline prompts.

**Create:**
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/setup.go` — `RunSetup` function + role/skills form constructors (the body of `entire review setup`). Also home to `invokerOnlyReviewConfig` (used by `entire review` for the non-interactive no-config path — defaults to ONLY the invoking agent as Both, not all installed launchable agents) so the fallback logic lives next to the interactive picker logic.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/setup_test.go` — picker validation, role normalization, save behavior. Includes `SetExistingConfigForTest` helper (writes a temp settings file inside a `t.TempDir()` repo).
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/roles.go` — package-private helpers: `NormalizeRoles`, `MigrateLegacyRoles` (thin wrapper around `settings`'s package-private helper for symmetric testing), `ReviewersOf`, `FixerOf`.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/roles_test.go` — table-driven tests for the helpers.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/post_review.go` — end-of-run UX: `RunPostReviewFixPrompt`, `printFindingsFooter`, `launchFixFromManifest`, `findingsCount`, `askPerRunPrompt`. Keeps `cmd.go` focused on dispatch.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/post_review_test.go` — branch coverage for `[Y]/[s]/[n]/[A]`, non-TTY, and always-mode paths.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/inline_prompt.go` — `ReadSingleKey` helper for one-keypress prompts.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/inline_prompt_test.go` — non-TTY fallback, default behavior, case-insensitivity, unknown-key swallow.
- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/migration.go` — package-private `migrateLegacyRoles` (the canonical implementation).
- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/stream_with_deltas.jsonl` — fixture with 2 assistant deltas + result envelope.
- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/stream_with_item_usage.jsonl` — fixture with 2 item.completed envelopes carrying running usage + turn.completed.

**Test conventions (apply throughout):**
- All new tests call `t.Parallel()` unless they mutate process-global state (env, cwd).
- Tests touching git state use `testutil.InitRepo(t, dir)` per CLAUDE.md.
- Subprocesses spawned from tests use `execx.NonInteractive` per CLAUDE.md.
- Test files include a complete `import` block at the top (the snippets below intentionally omit the block — assume the implementer adds standard imports + the packages referenced in the snippet).

